<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 20px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Wellness and Mindfulness – Lesson # 1</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Lesson #:</b> 1</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Skills Focus:</b> Listening</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Grade:</b> 9th Grade (CEFR: A2.4)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Scenario:</b> Wellness and Mindfulness</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Theme:</b> The Benefits of Mindfulness</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Specific Objective:</b> Listening: Receptive: Follow instructions in educational videos. Interactive: Respond to questions in group discussions.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Learning Outcome:</b> Listening: Can follow instructions in educational videos on exercise routines (e.g., "Demonstrate a stretching routine often used before school sports events.") Can respond to questions in discussions about wellness habits (e.g., "I practice mindfulness because it helps me relax and focus better on my studies. It makes me feel calm and peaceful.") Can answer questions about the benefits of mindfulness (e.g., "Relaxation is important because it reduces stress and makes you feel better.").</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f0f0f0; color: #1a5276; width: 35%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f0f0f0; color: #1a5276; width: 50%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f0f0f0; color: #1a5276; width: 15%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification of initial vocabulary related to "The Benefits of Mindfulness."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays a series of images showing different wellness activities (e.g., a person meditating, someone stretching, someone taking a deep breath). Students observe the images silently for 30 seconds. The teacher then asks open-ended questions like, "What are these people doing?" and "How do you think they feel?" encouraging brief oral responses to activate prior knowledge about wellness. Key vocabulary to elicit: <i>relax, exercise, calm</i>.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher introduces the terms <i>mindfulness</i> and <i>benefits</i>. The teacher says, "This person is practicing <b>mindfulness</b>. It has many <b>benefits</b> for your <b>health</b>." The teacher models pronunciation, emphasizing stress in 'mindfulness' and 'benefits'. The teacher uses gestures for 'calm' and 'focus'.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is <i>mindfulness</i> about being busy or being present and aware?" (Expected answer: Being present/aware)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Do <i>benefits</i> mean good things or bad things?" (Expected answer: Good things)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(8-10 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language and content related to the scenario "Wellness and Mindfulness" through a listening activity.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short (2-3 minute) educational video segment demonstrating basic mindfulness exercises (e.g., deep breathing, simple stretching) and briefly explaining their positive effects. The genre is educational video instructions/explanation, register is informative, and the format is audio-visual. The video contains phrases like "We are going to stretch our arms," "You are practicing deep breathing," and "Mindfulness helps to improve your focus."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Engage in group discussions on wellness routines, contributing suggestions and solutions to promote mental and physical well-being.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Listening (First Playback):</b> Students listen to the video for the main idea. The teacher asks, "What is the video mainly about: learning a new sport or understanding how to feel better?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False (Second Playback):</b> Students listen again and decide if statements are True or False based on the video. Examples: "Mindfulness makes you feel stressed." (False) "Stretching improves your body's flexibility." (True) "Breathing deeply can boost your energy." (True)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information Matching (Third Playback):</b> Students listen to specific instructions/benefits mentioned in the video and match them to images or short phrases (e.g., Match 'deep breathing' to 'calm and peaceful feeling'; 'stretching' to 'flexibility').</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(12-15 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on listening skills, consolidating target grammar (Present Simple, Present Continuous) and core vocabulary (wellness, mindfulness, benefits, relax, focus, calm, peaceful, boost, improve, stretch, breathe).</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Grammar:</b> Present continuous for ongoing actions ("I am practicing mindfulness."), Present simple for general statements ("Mindfulness has many benefits."). Collocations with health-related verbs ("energy boost").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Vocabulary:</b> wellness, mindfulness, exercise, energy, benefits, relaxation, focus, calm, peaceful, boost, improve, stretch, breathe.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pronunciation:</b> Focus on stress in multisyllabic words (e.g., "mindfulness," "flexibility," "resilience"). Practice distinguishing long and short vowels in minimal pairs (e.g., /ʊ/ in "could" versus /uː/ in "cooed," /ʊ/ in "soot" versus /uː/ in "suit").</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Listening Gap-fill:</b> Students receive a worksheet with sentences from the video or similar short descriptions of wellness activities, but with key target vocabulary words missing. The teacher plays short audio snippets (from the video or pre-recorded descriptions), and students listen carefully to fill in the blanks. (e.g., "She is ______ deeply to feel more ______." - <i>breathing, calm</i>). The teacher pauses after each snippet for students to write.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Sentence Scramble & Listen Check:</b> The teacher writes scrambled sentences on the board (e.g., "mindfulness / focus / improves / your") or projects them. Students work in pairs to unscramble them. Then, the teacher plays an audio recording of the correct, clear sentences, focusing on pronunciation, especially word stress ("Mindfulness improves your *focus*."). Students listen and check their answers for accuracy and pronunciation. The teacher uses a minimal pair drill: "He could wear a suit to the meeting." "He cooed at the baby while cleaning the soot from the chimney." Students listen and repeat.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Listen & Respond (Pair Work):</b> In pairs, Student A reads a sentence aloud describing a wellness habit, using target vocabulary and applying correct stress (e.g., "Daily <i>exercise</i> can <i>boost</i> your <i>energy</i>."). Student B listens and responds with a sentence about a potential benefit using the present simple, reinforcing vocabulary (e.g., "Yes, exercise <i>improves</i> physical <i>health</i> and helps you <i>relax</i>."). They switch roles after 2-3 sentences.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(15-18 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students use the language actively in a realistic scenario, focusing on listening and responding.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Small group discussion (3-4 students). Each group receives a set of discussion prompts related to wellness and mindfulness. Students actively listen to their peers' contributions and respond.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher provides discussion questions written on cards or projected, such as: "What wellness practices do you *feel* are most important for teens?" "How does practicing <i>mindfulness</i> help you *focus* on your studies?" "Can you describe a time when you felt very <i>calm</i> and <i>peaceful</i>?" "What are the *benefits* of daily <i>exercise</i>?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students take turns reading a question aloud. All group members *listen carefully* to the question and then share their ideas, using the target vocabulary (<i>wellness, mindfulness, benefits, relax, focus, calm, peaceful, boost, improve</i>) and the present simple/continuous where appropriate.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">They are encouraged to respond to each other's points (e.g., "I agree with [name], <i>relaxation</i> is important because it reduces stress and makes you *feel* better," or "Some people like to <i>meditate</i> because it helps them manage stress."). The teacher circulates, monitoring for active listening, use of target language, and pronunciation.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(8-10 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment of listening comprehension and interactive responses during the group discussion.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist during the group discussion.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students' participation and responses in the group discussion from Stage 4.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Listening and Interaction Focus):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Listens actively:</b> (e.g., Responds appropriately to peers' statements, asks clarifying questions).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Understands instructions:</b> (e.g., Follows group discussion prompts correctly).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Intelligible pronunciation:</b> (e.g., Clear stress in multisyllabic words like "mindfulness," "flexibility").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Uses target vocabulary:</b> (e.g., Incorporates "wellness," "mindfulness," "benefits," "relax," "focus," "calm," "peaceful" correctly).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Responds to questions clearly:</b> (e.g., Provides coherent answers to discussion questions).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete two sentences on a small slip of paper.</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One new benefit of mindfulness I learned today is ______."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Today, I understood most of the information because ______."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(5 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Review of the lesson's effectiveness and planning for future lessons.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How well did I understand the instructions in the video and my group members' ideas today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What new vocabulary or pronunciation (e.g., 'flexibility,' 'mindfulness') did I learn that helps me talk about wellness?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What aspects of the lesson effectively facilitated listening comprehension and the introduction of new vocabulary?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">How could I better support students in identifying stress in multisyllabic words or distinguishing vowel sounds for more accurate listening? What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for the next lesson?</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> "Today we focused on listening to understand the benefits of mindfulness. Next lesson, we will continue exploring this theme by *reading* an article about how mindfulness can *improve* academic performance, using many of the same vocabulary words we learned today."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(2 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>